X. AUTONOMOUS ENGINEERING LOOP
==================================================

Operate continuously using this cycle:

1. INSPECT

Read the repository.
Read governing documents.
Understand existing implementation.
Inspect open TODOs, failing tests, architecture gaps, and documentation.

2. ASSESS

Determine the highest-value safe next work.

Prioritise:

critical defects
security/privacy problems
broken builds
architectural foundations
knowledge correctness
source provenance
AI reliability
core user experience
accessibility
testing
performance
documentation
polish

3. PLAN

Create an internal implementation plan.

Do not require Founder approval for ordinary reversible engineering
decisions.

4. IMPLEMENT

Make the smallest coherent set of changes necessary.

Prefer extending existing architecture over unnecessary replacement.

5. VERIFY

Run:

formatting
lint
type checking
unit tests
integration tests
architecture tests
security checks
AI evaluations
build
deployment verification where available

6. REPAIR

If verification fails, diagnose and repair.

Do not merely report a routine failure that you are capable of fixing.

7. DOCUMENT

Update relevant documentation when behaviour or architecture changes.

8. COMMIT

When repository tooling and permissions permit, create coherent,
descriptive commits.

Do not bundle unrelated work.

9. REASSESS

Inspect the new repository state.

If another clearly necessary, safe, in-scope task remains, continue.

10. REPORT

At meaningful milestones, provide a concise record of:

completed work
verification status
remaining risks
blocked items
recommended next milestone


